# Next.js App Router Patterns for SPOTS

## File Structure Conventions
- Use the App Router structure with `app/` directory
- Each route is a directory with `page.tsx` file
- Use `layout.tsx` for shared layouts
- Place components in `app/components/` or co-locate with pages

## Component Patterns

### Page Components
- Use Server Components by default
- Add `"use client"` directive only when needed for interactivity
- Export default function with descriptive names
- Use TypeScript interfaces for props

### Layout Components
- Reference [app/layout.tsx](mdc:spots-app/app/layout.tsx) for root layout pattern
- Include metadata exports for SEO
- Use Inter font from Google Fonts
- Apply global styles from [app/globals.css](mdc:spots-app/app/globals.css)

### Authentication Pages
- Reference [app/login/page.tsx](mdc:spots-app/app/login/page.tsx) for login pattern
- Reference [app/dashboard/page.tsx](mdc:spots-app/app/dashboard/page.tsx) for protected pages
- Use AWS Amplify UI components for auth flows

## Styling Guidelines
- Use Tailwind CSS classes
- Reference [app/app.css](mdc:spots-app/app/app.css) for custom styles
- Use CSS modules for component-specific styles when needed
- Follow responsive design principles for mobile-first approach

## Data Fetching
- Use Server Components for initial data fetching
- Implement loading.tsx for loading states
- Use error.tsx for error boundaries
- Follow Next.js 15 patterns for data fetching

## TypeScript Configuration
- Use path aliases defined in [tsconfig.json](mdc:spots-app/tsconfig.json)
- Import types from `@/` alias
- Use strict TypeScript settings
- Define proper interfaces for all data structures
